    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d863">

                <pb facs="0147" n="1529" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v13p2/pg1529"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/5–1054: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        France</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d863-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-10T21:00:00-04:00">May 10, 1954—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4017. Eyes only for Ambassador from Secretary.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Reur 4287,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d863-f2"/> Laniel raises two questions:
                            (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) Whether we will send general officer to
                        discuss regrouping of French forces in Indochina; and (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">b</hi>) under what conditions US might intervene in
                        Indochina. This cable answers question (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>).
                        Will send answer to (<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>) tomorrow.<anchor n="3"
                            xml:id="d863-f3"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>If Assembly supports Cabinet in Indochina debate starting Tuesday,<anchor
                            n="4" xml:id="d863-f4"/> US will send general officer to Paris for
                        discussion with Laniel, Pleven and Ely as requested. Tentatively expected to
                        be Trapnell. All <pb facs="0148" n="1530" xml:id="pg1530"/> publicity should
                        be avoided, if possible. To provide cover, if needed, his visit may be
                        treated as related to preparation of military aid program for coming year.
                        Officer will deal only with military aspects. You will handle all other
                        aspects and will feel free to accompany him on his discussions.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>You should make it perfectly clear to Laniel that our response to his
                        request is due to our desire to be helpful and that general officer would
                        give his best personal judgment on specific inquiries, but he will not in
                        any way engage the responsibility of the US. In particular his participation
                        in French discussions does not imply any future commitment to
                            intervene.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d863-f5"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d863-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d863-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by the Secretary of State. Repeated to Geneva as Tedul 53, for the eyes
                    of Under Secretary Smith only.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d863-f2" n="2" xml:id="d863-f2-content">
                <p>Dated May 10, <ref target="#pg1522">p. 1522</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d863-f3" n="3" xml:id="d863-f3-content">
                <p>See telegram 4023 to Paris, May 11, <ref target="#pg1534">p. 1534</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d863-f4" n="4" xml:id="d863-f4-content">
                <p>May 11.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d863-f5" n="5" xml:id="d863-f5-content">
                <p>In telegram 4309 from Paris, May 11, Ambassador Dillon stated the following: “I
                    informed Laniel this morning of answer to question (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >a</hi>) contained Deptel 4017. In this connection I stressed paragraph 3 of
                    reference telegram and Laniel replied that he understood perfectly and that his
                    immediate desire under question (<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>) was to
                    obtaining the best possible military advice. He realizes fully that there is no
                    implication of any future commitment and he is very grateful for prompt reply.”
                    (751G.00/5–1154)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
